       "severity": "Medium",
       "description": "Summary: Multiple vulnerabilities have been identified in the libxml2 library, a development toolbox for XML standards. These include an integer overflow in the xmlBuildQName function (CVE-2025-6021), leading to a stack-based buffer overflow, memory corruption, or denial of service when processing crafted input. Other issues include out-of-bounds read (CVE-2025-32414), heap use-after-free (CVE-2025-49794), and type confusion (CVE-2025-49796), all potentially resulting in denial of service. Impact: Exploitation of these vulnerabilities could lead to memory corruption, application crashes, or denial of service, impacting system stability and security. AdditionalInformation: The vulnerabilities affect libxml2 versions less than 2.10.4-8 and 2.11.5-6. For detailed information, refer to the respective CVE pages. Remediation: Apply the latest patches and updates provided by the respective vendors. [Generated by AI]",
